  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left|\\frac{z-3 i}{z+3 i}\\right|=1 \\Rightarrow|z-3 i|=|z+3 i|$\r\n\r\n[if $\\left|z-z_{1}\\right|=\\left|z+z_{2}\\right|,$ then it is a perpendicular bisector of $z_{1}$ and $z_{2}$ ] Hence, perpendicular bisector of (0,3) and (0,-3) is $X$ -axis.",
